# Answer key for M2 (m2_shipment_exceptions.sql): the shipment exception board.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE (2026-10-07).
# CLOSED WORLD: every <result> column and every filter is stated. Conventions D-1..D-53.
#
# Row-deciding path: hdr (DISTINCT ON) JOIN ln -> base, the final WHERE, the final LIMIT.
# late_lines, carrier_perf and customer_rank read base, which is on the main path: base's own
# predicates stay filters there only; each CTE's OWN WHERE is a value of what it feeds,
# aggregated where the CTE aggregates (D-45). The alias `cr` is customer_rank in the outer
# FROM and lgx.carrier inside the WHERE's IN: the inner one shadows.

@ 22 the whole statement

# --- plain columns ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
value lgx.shipment_line.shipment_line_id -> <result>.shipment_line_id identity
value lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.shipment_id identity
value lgx.shipment_header.customer_id -> <result>.customer_id identity

# --- SELECT-list subqueries (D-12, D-13) -------------------------------------------------------
value crm.customer.customer_name -> <result>.customer_name identity
# D-58: crm.customer.customer_id, lgx.shipment_header.customer_id -> <result>.customer_name is a lookup key (join_key, not scored; was a conditional value).
value crm.contact.email -> <result>.primary_email identity
# D-58: crm.contact.customer_id, lgx.shipment_header.customer_id -> <result>.primary_email is a lookup key (join_key, not scored; was a conditional value).
influence crm.contact.is_primary, crm.contact.created_at -> <result>.primary_email
value lgx.package_event.event_type -> <result>.exception_count aggregated
# D-58: lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id matched the aggregated lookup's rows to <result>.exception_count's - influence, as a GROUP BY is (was a value).
influence lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.exception_count
value lgx.package_event.event_ts -> <result>.last_scan_ts aggregated
# D-58: lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id matched the aggregated lookup's rows to <result>.last_scan_ts's - influence, as a GROUP BY is (was a value).
influence lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.last_scan_ts
value lgx.package_event.event_type -> <result>.is_delivered conditional
# D-58: lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.is_delivered is a lookup key (join_key, not scored; was a conditional value).
value lgx.shipment_line.item_id, lgx.item_master.item_id, lgx.item_master.item_class -> <result>.hazmat_lines aggregated
# D-58: lgx.shipment_line.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id matched the aggregated lookup's rows to <result>.hazmat_lines's - influence, as a GROUP BY is (was a value).
influence lgx.shipment_line.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.hazmat_lines
note The IN nested inside the counting subquery decides a value, not a row: every column of it is an aggregated value (D-45), never a filter.
forbid filter lgx.item_master.item_class -> <result> | an IN inside a SELECT-list scalar subquery removes no result row (D-12, D-45)

# --- LEFT JOIN LATERAL le: last non-NOTE event (D-14) ------------------------------------------
value lgx.package_event.event_type -> <result>.last_event_type conditional
# D-58: lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.last_event_type is a lookup key (join_key, not scored; was a conditional value).
note event_type is projected AND tested in the lateral's WHERE: one fact at the hardest transform (D-51).
value lgx.package_event.event_ts -> <result>.last_event_ts identity
value lgx.package_event.location_code -> <result>.last_location identity
value lgx.package_event.event_type -> <result>.last_event_ts conditional
value lgx.package_event.event_type -> <result>.last_location conditional
# D-58: lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.last_event_ts is a lookup key (join_key, not scored; was a conditional value).
# D-58: lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.last_location is a lookup key (join_key, not scored; was a conditional value).
influence lgx.package_event.event_ts -> <result>.last_event_type, <result>.last_event_ts, <result>.last_location
forbid filter lgx.package_event.event_type -> <result> | a one-row LEFT LATERAL removes no outer row (D-14)

# --- LEFT JOIN LATERAL fx: latest USD rate (D-14) -----------------------------------------------
value gold.fx_rate.conversion_rate -> <result>.usd_rate identity
value lgx.shipment_line.shipped_qty, lgx.shipment_line.unit_selling_price, gold.fx_rate.conversion_rate -> <result>.ext_amount_usd derived
value gold.fx_rate.to_ccy -> <result>.usd_rate conditional
value gold.fx_rate.to_ccy -> <result>.ext_amount_usd conditional
# D-58: gold.fx_rate.from_ccy, gold.fx_rate.rate_date, lgx.shipment_header.currency_code, lgx.shipment_line.ship_date -> <result>.usd_rate is a lookup key (join_key, not scored; was a conditional value).
# D-58: gold.fx_rate.from_ccy, gold.fx_rate.rate_date, lgx.shipment_header.currency_code, lgx.shipment_line.ship_date -> <result>.ext_amount_usd is a lookup key (join_key, not scored; was a conditional value).
influence gold.fx_rate.rate_date -> <result>.usd_rate, <result>.ext_amount_usd
forbid filter gold.fx_rate.rate_date -> <result> | a one-row LEFT LATERAL removes no outer row (D-14)

# --- late_lines (own WHERE: aggregated values) -------------------------------------------------
value lgx.shipment_line.ship_date, lgx.shipment_line.promise_date -> <result>.late_line_count, <result>.worst_delay_days aggregated
influence lgx.shipment_header.customer_id -> <result>.late_line_count, <result>.worst_delay_days

# --- flagged_customers (EXISTS + NOT IN (... EXCEPT ...), all values under D-45) ----------------
value crm.customer.segment -> <result>.flagged_segment identity
value crm.customer.customer_id, evt.flag.entity_id, evt.flag.active_flag, crm.contact.customer_id, crm.contact.role, crm.contact.is_primary -> <result>.flagged_segment, <result>.is_flagged conditional
note is_flagged = fc.customer_id IS NOT NULL: derived from customer_id directly, conditional through the sweep; one fact at the hardest (D-51).
forbid filter crm.contact.role -> <result> | flagged_customers is reached only through a LEFT join (D-45, D-52 as values)
forbid filter evt.flag.active_flag -> <result> | flagged_customers is reached only through a LEFT join (D-45)

# --- risk_class: CASE over late_line_count and fc.customer_id -------------------------------------
value lgx.shipment_line.ship_date, lgx.shipment_line.promise_date -> <result>.risk_class aggregated
value crm.customer.customer_id, evt.flag.entity_id, evt.flag.active_flag, crm.contact.customer_id, crm.contact.role, crm.contact.is_primary -> <result>.risk_class conditional
influence lgx.shipment_header.customer_id -> <result>.risk_class

# --- carrier_perf (own WHERE promise_date IS NOT NULL: aggregated value) -----------------------
value lgx.shipment_line.ship_date, lgx.shipment_line.promise_date -> <result>.carrier_otd_ratio, <result>.carrier_p90_delay aggregated
influence lgx.shipment_header.carrier_code, lgx.shipment_line.ship_date -> <result>.carrier_otd_ratio, <result>.carrier_p90_delay
note GROUP BY carrier_code, date_trunc('month', ship_date) (D-2); ship_date is also a value (D-47). The join on cp.perf_month = date_trunc(...) is a key equality (D-11).

# --- customer_rank: RANK over SUM ---------------------------------------------------------------
value lgx.shipment_line.shipped_qty, lgx.shipment_line.unit_selling_price -> <result>.customer_revenue aggregated
influence lgx.shipment_header.customer_id -> <result>.customer_revenue, <result>.customer_revenue_rank
influence lgx.shipment_line.shipped_qty, lgx.shipment_line.unit_selling_price -> <result>.customer_revenue_rank
note RANK() OVER (ORDER BY SUM(...)): the summed columns order it (D-4) and the GROUP BY behind the sum influences it (D-46).

# --- filters -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
filter lgx.shipment_header.is_deleted, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.version_no -> <result>
filter lgx.shipment_line.line_status -> <result>
filter lgx.shipment_header.carrier_code, lgx.carrier.carrier_code, lgx.carrier.active_flag, lgx.carrier_service.carrier_code, lgx.carrier_service.transit_days -> <result>
note IN over a UNION: both arms' match columns and WHERE columns (D-52).
filter crm.contact.customer_id, lgx.shipment_header.customer_id, crm.customer.customer_id, crm.customer.status -> <result>
note EXISTS over an INTERSECT: each arm's correlation and predicate (D-52).
filter lgx.shipment_line.item_id, lgx.bill_of_material.component_item_id, lgx.bill_of_material.bom_status -> <result>
note NOT (item_id = ANY (subquery)) is an anti-join (D-52).
filter lgx.shipment_line.unit_selling_price, lgx.item_master.std_cost, lgx.item_master.item_id -> <result>
note >= SOME with a correlation: the compared columns and the correlation (B2 S7, D-52).
filter lgx.shipment_line.shipment_line_id -> <result>
note ORDER BY shipment_id, shipment_line_id LIMIT 5000 (D-9); shipment_id is stated above.
